{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1562174503,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODE4MzIzNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510#issuecomment-508183237"},"message":"+1 for making it work, @satra would be interested as well ;)\n\nI am really surprised with `datalad get` failing somehow! there should be nothing remote specific.  Would you mind sharing/publishing that tiny sample repo somewhere?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562176913,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODE5NzIxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510#issuecomment-508197219"},"message":"\u003e +1 for making it work, @satra would be interested as well ;)\n\nAll right, more motivation for me to look into it :)\n\n\u003e I am really surprised with `datalad get` failing somehow! there should be nothing remote specific.\n\nYeah, I was too.\n\n\u003e Would you mind sharing/publishing that tiny sample repo somewhere?\n\nI wouldn't mind, but I think the script to generate it is more useful, so I've included that below.  I've also dumped the resulting repo on smaug at /tmp/gx-ipfs-e8l3B8I.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003escript\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```sh\n#!/bin/sh\n\n# Assumes you have git-annex-remote-ipfs on your path and the IPFS\n# daemon running.\n\nset -eux\n\ncd $(mktemp -dt gx-ipfs-XXXXXXX)\ngit init\ngit annex init\n\ngit annex initremote ipfs type=external externaltype=ipfs encryption=none\n\necho one \u003eone\ngit annex add one\ngit commit -mone\n\ngit annex copy --to ipfs one\ngit annex whereis one\n\ngit annex drop --force one\ngit annex whereis one\n\ngit annex get one\ngit annex whereis one\n\ngit annex drop --force one\ngit annex whereis one\n\ndatalad get one\ngit annex whereis one\n```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562179916,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODIwNzI2Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510#issuecomment-508207267"},"message":"\u003e \u003e I am really surprised with `datalad get` failing somehow! there should be nothing remote specific.\n\u003e \n\u003e Yeah, I was too.\n\nHmph looks like `datalad get` is may be behaving odd for me in general, and I incorrectly assumed it was related to the IPFS remote.  I'll need to debug more, but please don't waste any time troubleshooting on your end.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562179916,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI0NDY5ODE5NA=="},"target":"a2f54868119b22743a0f0e8345464fb190bb3fe48e6d825cb78cc95cf77b93c6","message":"\u003e \u003e I am really surprised with `datalad get` failing somehow! there should be nothing remote specific.\n\u003e \n\u003e Yeah, I was too.\n\nHmph looks like `datalad get` may be behaving odd for me in general, and I incorrectly assumed it was related to the IPFS remote.  I'll need to debug more, but please don't waste any time troubleshooting on your end.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562179929,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODIxMTczNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510#issuecomment-508211737"},"message":"\u003e Hmph looks like `datalad get` is may be behaving odd for me in general, and I incorrectly assumed it was related to the IPFS remote. I'll need to debug more, but please don't waste any time troubleshooting on your end.\n\nWith my git-annex (7.20190626), `annex find --json` isn't giving the expected output:\n\n```\n$ git annex find --json --not --in=here -- one\none\n```\n\nand that is what leads to DataLad thinking the file is available.\n\nIf I use the annex from neurodebian, things look fine, including getting from the IPFS special remote:\n\n```\n$ git annex find --json --not --in=here -- one\n{\"bytesize\":\"4\",\"mtime\":\"unknown\",\"keyname\":\"2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806\",\"backend\":\"SHA256E\",\"key\":\"SHA256E-s4--2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806\",\"humansize\":\"4 B\",\"hashdirmixed\":\"0J/J1/\",\"file\":\"one\",\"hashdirlower\":\"171/8dc/\"}\ndatalad get one\nget(ok): /tmp/gx-ipfs-px8wztj/one (file) [from ipfs...]\n```\n\nSo great, and sorry for the noise!\n\nI'll debug `git annex find --json` a bit more on my end, and open an issue upstream if appropriate.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562179929,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI0NDY5ODI4Ng=="},"target":"023c4d94e82edc0e0ce0eddc7c1d7bf96305ce185b46194d7e3e759382e2fb2f","message":"\u003e Hmph looks like `datalad get` may be behaving odd for me in general, and I incorrectly assumed it was related to the IPFS remote. I'll need to debug more, but please don't waste any time troubleshooting on your end.\n\nWith my git-annex (7.20190626), `annex find --json` isn't giving the expected output:\n\n```\n$ git annex find --json --not --in=here -- one\none\n```\n\nand that is what leads to DataLad thinking the file is available.\n\nIf I use the annex from neurodebian, things look fine, including getting from the IPFS special remote:\n\n```\n$ git annex find --json --not --in=here -- one\n{\"bytesize\":\"4\",\"mtime\":\"unknown\",\"keyname\":\"2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806\",\"backend\":\"SHA256E\",\"key\":\"SHA256E-s4--2c8b08da5ce60398e1f19af0e5dccc744df274b826abe585eaba68c525434806\",\"humansize\":\"4 B\",\"hashdirmixed\":\"0J/J1/\",\"file\":\"one\",\"hashdirlower\":\"171/8dc/\"}\ndatalad get one\nget(ok): /tmp/gx-ipfs-px8wztj/one (file) [from ipfs...]\n```\n\nSo great, and sorry for the noise!\n\nI'll debug `git annex find --json` a bit more on my end, and open an issue upstream if appropriate.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562179361,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjQ1ODUwOTAzMA=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1562182515,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODIyODA3MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510#issuecomment-508228071"},"message":"lets keep it open may be for ipfs?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562182771,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODIyOTI0Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510#issuecomment-508229246"},"message":"\u003e lets keep it open may be for ipfs?\n\nWhat about it?  If you want something specific on DataLad's end (a pointer in the documentation?), I think a new, dedicated issue would be better.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1562183508,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODIzMjY4OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510#issuecomment-508232688"},"message":"\u003e I'll debug `git annex find --json` a bit more on my end, and open an issue upstream if appropriate.\n\nFor posterity: \u003chttps://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/Regression_in___96__find_--json__96___output/\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1562184371,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODIzNjkxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3510#issuecomment-508236916"},"message":"Heh heh heh -- thank you @kyleam !","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"b6514b9b57c47fbb79fc9d0864ed8b5f63682d4e"},"timestamp":1562377829,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwODg4ODY1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/i